hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1526","This is Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar, this is Yahya, Al-Hajjaj told us. Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa`id al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Abi Uthman al-Sawwaf. H Ahmad bin Abdah narrated to us, Sufyan, meaning Ibn Habib, narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj al-Sawaf, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the prayer is established, do not stand until ""You see me."" Ahmad ibn Sinan said: He said: “When the muezzin announces the call to prayer, do not get up until you see me.”"
